{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794520261,"nonce":"3PKU2MWUW5hlth/+fD7DSPR85eQ=","title":"Android: build and run an ash program with only the Android SDK and NDK installed","message":"Requirement (owner, 2026-11-12): Android-specific support and tooling, so a developer needs little setup beyond the Android SDK.\n\nChecked 2026-11-12 on a Mac with NDK 27 and 29 and the Rust Android targets installed:\n- The compiler already emits objects: `ash --emit-aot out.o --target \u003ctriple\u003e` gives ELF for aarch64-linux-android, armv7-linux-androideabi and x86_64-linux-android from test_basic.hl.\n- The runtime does not build as shipped: `cargo check -p ash_std --target aarch64-linux-android` stops in std/build.rs (header discovery) with \"no cross compiler was found ... tried aarch64-linux-android-gcc\". It looks for `\u003ctriple\u003e-gcc`, which neither the NDK nor Android Studio provides.\n- With `BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS_aarch64_linux_android=\"--target=aarch64-linux-android24 --sysroot=\u003cndk\u003e/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/darwin-x86_64/sysroot\"` the same check finishes. It reports 10 improper_ctypes warnings, all the generated `va_list` as `[u64; 4]`.\n\nNot checked: linking, running anything on a device or emulator, armv7 and x86_64 runtime builds, how the fiber switch, setjmp traps, signals and unwinding behave on bionic, dlopen of HDLLs, stdout reaching logcat.\n\nMissing today: release.yml builds no runtime for an Android triple; the native cross link in aot_link.rs names darwin, linux and windows and has no NDK discovery; there is no packaging step.\n\nAcceptance, from the requirement:\n1. Find the NDK without configuration: ANDROID_NDK_HOME / ANDROID_NDK_ROOT, then ANDROID_HOME/ndk/\u003cnewest\u003e, then the platform default SDK location; the host tag; a default minimum API level, overridable.\n2. std/build.rs takes the target's headers from the NDK sysroot with no gcc and no env var.\n3. A runtime per Android ABI (arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a, x86_64) in the release archives, found by triple like the other cross runtimes.\n4. `ash --build --target \u003candroid triple\u003e` links with the NDK's clang and lld and writes a loadable shared library.\n5. A way to get from that library to something that runs: decide whether that is an APK, a Gradle project template, or only the .so for a developer's own project. Open question for the owner.\n6. `ash run` on an emulator or device through adb, with output in logcat; a CI job that does it on an emulator.\n\nShared with the iOS issue: a C entry point for starting the runtime from a host app, and the per-target runtimes in the release workflow.","files":null}]}